      en: "St. George's Church in Petrinja is a Serbian Orthodox church built in 1782 in the late baroque style. Its iconostasis, carved in 1790, features icons influenced by the Macedonian school. During the 1991 war, the church was shelled and its roof collapsed. Restoration efforts from 1995 to 2000 repaired the structure and restored the iconostasis. The churchyard contains a well from 1880 and graves of notable local Serbs. Services are held weekly, and the parish has around 1,500 members. The church is listed as a protected cultural monument.",
