      en: "St. Michael's Fortress in Šibenik was built by the Venetians in the 15th century atop a 70-meter hill. It features four bastions and a dry moat. The fortress withstood an Ottoman siege in 1647. After being abandoned in the 19th century, it later served as a barracks. Restoration in the 2000s transformed it into a cultural venue with an open-air stage seating 1,000. The fortress offers panoramic views of Šibenik and the Adriatic. It is considered one of the best-preserved Venetian fortifications in Dalmatia.",
