      en: "The Museum of Broken Relationships in Zagreb is a unique museum featuring personal objects from failed relationships. Founded in 2006 by artists Olinka Vištica and Dražen Grubišić, the exhibits are donated anonymously and tell stories of love, loss, and memory. Housed in the upper floor of the Baroque Kulmer Palace in the old town, it gained global recognition and won the Kenneth Hudson Award in 2011 for the most innovative museum in Europe.",
